Changes beginning October 24, 2026 include independent project/release metadata,
an embedded corresponding-source offer, and downstream reliability work. Git
history records individual modifications and their dates. Runtime command names
and OUTPACE_* configuration variables are retained for compatibility.

Each distributed engine binary embeds its own workspace source archive. Run
    outpace source > source.tar.gz
or download /source.tar.gz from its HTTP server. /source and /source.json provide
license/source links and build identity. A Git base revision alone does not
identify a modified build; use the archive's SHA-256 and SOURCE-MANIFEST.json.

Official release binaries also link to a complete source asset identified by
version, target and Git revision. It contains the exact embedded workspace
archive, every locked Rust registry dependency, original third-party notices,
and offline rebuild instructions. THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt accompanies the binary
and the published runtime image. Local modified builds require their own matching
complete source bundle; they do not advertise an unrelated release asset.

Third-party dependencies retain their respective licenses. Cargo.lock records
exact Rust dependency versions and registry checksums. An optional separately
installed FFmpeg has its own build-dependent licensing terms.

